# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — keep the Docker build context small AND secure
# =============================================================================
# LESSON: Module 0 / Module 8 (Security).
# SECURITY: anything listed here is NOT sent to the Docker daemon during a
#   build, which means it can never accidentally end up baked into an image
#   layer. We exclude secrets (.env), local state (.venv, *.db), and git
#   history (.git) — none of which belong in a production image.
# =============================================================================

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite3
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
docs/
.github/
